<title>CHINA: GM buys China equipment for Thai project.</title>
<headline>GM buys China equipment for Thai project.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said on Friday it had agreed to buy three stamping lines worth $26.7 million from China for use at its auto assembly plant under construction in Thailand.</p>
<p>GM's Beijing office said the purchase agreement was signed this week with the state-run China National Heavy Machinery Corp.</p>
<p>General Motors is investing $750 million to build an assembly plant in Thailand's eastern Rayong province. The plant will produce 100,000 cars a year from early 1999.</p>
<p>Thailand was chosen over the Phlippines as the site for the plant in a hotly contested race.</p>
</text>
